08'!renderOneFrameToScreen	"Render one single frame and display it"	"Ah, I see a mistake. A sprite can have multiple bitmaps. Just call the base class a sprite""But the next thing is, maybe I shouldn't have broken up the base class?""My thinking is that a character sprite, or object sprite, will have one-or-more static bitmaps, not a single color form that is constantly updated""Also will want to draw multiple of the same sprite, without having to have multiple instances of this object, like for bricks.""For RealtimeFire, yes, I want separate sprites, so they each are a little different""So I don't see any benefit to subclassing from AbstractDynamicSprite to DynamicBitmapSprite"self shouldNotImplement.! !Object subclass: #Array2D	instanceVariableNames: 'arr'	classVariableNames: ''	poolDictionaries: ''	category: 'FlamesRefactor'!!Array2D methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 4/1/2020 13:19'!at: x at: y	"comment stating purpose of message"	^ (arr at: y) at: x.! !!Array2D methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 4/1/2020 13:18'!at: x at: y put: val	"comment stating purpose of message"	 (arr at: y) at: x put: val.! !!Array2D methodsFor: 'initialize-release' stamp: 'jmi 3/25/2021 11:20'!initializeFrom: array2d	"comment stating purpose of message""	height := array2d size.	firstRow := array2d at: 1.	width := firstRow size.		1 to: height do: [:i|		currentRow := array2d at: i.		currentRow size = width ifFalse: [^false]		]."	(self class isValid: array2d) ifFalse: [self invalid].	arr := array2d.! !!Array2D methodsFor: 'initialize-release' stamp: 'jmi 4/1/2020 13:18'!width: w height: h type: klass	"comment stating purpose of message"	arr := Array new: h.	1 to: h do: [:i|		arr at: i put: (klass new: w).		].! !"-- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- "!Array2D class	instanceVariableNames: ''!!Array2D class methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 3/25/2021 10:43'!createFrom: array2d	"Construct a new Array2d from a literal 2d array""	| pThis |		pThis := Array2D new: w.	pThis arr: (Array new: h).	1 to: h do: [:i|		arr at: i put: (klass new: w).		]."! !!Array2D class methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 3/26/2021 14:02'!isValid: array2d	"Validate whether this is a valid construction of a 2d array"	| height width |	height := array2d size.	height <= 0 ifTrue: [^false].	width := (array2d at: 1) size.	width <= 0 ifTrue: [^false].	"	1 to: height do: [:i|		currentRow := array2d at: i.		 size = width ifFalse: [^false]		]."		array2d do: [:row|		row size = width ifFalse: [^false].		].^ true.! !!Array2D class methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 4/1/2020 01:06'!newWidth: w height: h type: klass	"comment stating purpose of message""	| pThis |		pThis := Array2D new: w.	pThis arr: (Array new: h).	1 to: h do: [:i|		arr at: i put: (klass new: w).		]."! !Object subclass: #ColorRange	instanceVariableNames: 'color range'	classVariableNames: ''	poolDictionaries: ''	category: 'FlamesRefactor'!!ColorRange methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 4/1/2020 11:26'!color	"comment stating purpose of message"	^ color! !!ColorRange methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 4/1/2020 11:27'!color: theColor	"comment stating purpose of message"	color := theColor! !!ColorRange methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 4/1/2020 11:27'!range	"comment stating purpose of message"	^ range! !!ColorRange methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 4/1/2020 11:27'!range: theRange	"comment stating purpose of message"	range := theRange! !"-- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- "!ColorRange class	instanceVariableNames: ''!!ColorRange class methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 4/1/2020 11:44'!color: c range: r	"comment stating purpose of message"	^ ColorRange new color: c; range: r.! !Object subclass: #CoolingStrategy	instanceVariableNames: ''	classVariableNames: ''	poolDictionaries: ''	category: 'FlamesRefactor'!!CoolingStrategy commentStamp: 'jmi 3/22/2021 20:41' prior: 0!A CoolingStrategy is how to slowly decay or "cool" the colors on screen.CoolingStrategy is the base class for various strategies for decaying the colors on the screenInstance Variables!]style[(73 94 21),c186063063,!!CoolingStrategy methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 3/22/2021 23:52'!at: x at: y	"Abstract base class does not implement this. Derived class must provide an implementation"	^ self subclassResponsibility.! !!CoolingStrategy methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 3/23/2021 15:48'!progressOneFrame	"Abstract base class does not implement this. Derived classshould provide an implementation if desired to update things once per frame"	^ self.! !CoolingStrategy subclass: #CoolingStrategyConst	instanceVariableNames: 'coolingFactor'	classVariableNames: ''	poolDictionaries: ''	category: 'FlamesRefactor'!!CoolingStrategyConst commentStamp: 'jmi 3/22/2021 20:42' prior: 0!A CoolingStrategyConst is xxxxxxxxx.Simple cooling strategy to always subtract the same amountInstance Variables	coolingFactor:		<Object>coolingFactor	- xxxxx!]style[(38 58 71),c186063063,!!CoolingStrategyConst methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 3/22/2021 19:02'!at: x at: y	^ coolingFactor. "Constant cooling factor never changes"! !!CoolingStrategyConst methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 3/22/2021 19:00'!setCoolingFactor: cf	"initialize"	coolingFactor := cf.! !"-- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- "!CoolingStrategyConst class	instanceVariableNames: ''!!CoolingStrategyConst class methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 3/22/2021 19:03'!create: coolingFactor	"comment stating purpose of message"	^ self new setCoolingFactor: coolingFactor.! !CoolingStrategy subclass: #CoolingStrategyMap	instanceVariableNames: 'map random width height rotate shift density min max smoothing iCoolingOffset iFrame'	classVariableNames: ''	poolDictionaries: ''	category: 'FlamesRefactor'!!CoolingStrategyMap methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 3/23/2021 23:47'!at: x at: y	^ map at: (x + (y * width) + iCoolingOffset - 1) \\ (width * height) + 1.! !!CoolingStrategyMap methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 3/23/2021 23:31'!fillCoolingMap: coolingMap start: start end: end	start to: end do: [:i|		coolingMap at: i put: 0.		(random nextInt: 100) < density ifTrue: [			coolingMap at: i put: min + (random nextInt: (max-min + 1)) - 1.			].		].! !!CoolingStrategyMap methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 3/23/2021 20:35'!initialize	random := Random new.	iCoolingOffset := 0.	iFrame := 0.! !!CoolingStrategyMap methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 3/23/2021 20:29'!initializeCoolingMap	"initialize"	| size |	size := height * width.	map ifNil: [map := Array new: size].	self fillCoolingMap: map start: 1 end: size.		self smoothCoolingMap: smoothing.! !!CoolingStrategyMap methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 3/23/2021 23:46'!progressOneFrame	"rotate the cooling map"		shift ifFalse: [		iFrame := 0.		iCoolingOffset := 0.		] ifTrue: [		iFrame := iFrame + 1.		"if ()iFrame > height) updateCoolingMap."		iCoolingOffset := (width * iFrame) \\ (width * height).		].		rotate & (iFrame > height) ifTrue: [		self fillCoolingMap: map start: iCoolingOffset + 1 end: width.		].! !!CoolingStrategyMap methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 3/23/2021 20:01'!setWidth: w height: h rotate: bRotate shift: bShift density: nDensity min: nMin max: nMax smoothing: nSmoothing	"initialize"	width := w.	height := h.	rotate := bRotate.	shift := bShift.	density := nDensity.	min := nMin.	max := nMax.	smoothing := nSmoothing.	self initializeCoolingMap.! !!CoolingStrategyMap methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 3/23/2021 19:54'!smoothCoolingMap: iterations	"initialize"	| destMap tempSwap |	destMap := Array new: map size.		1 to: iterations do: [:x|		self smoothCoolingMap: map destination: destMap.		tempSwap := map.		map := destMap.		destMap := tempSwap.		tempSwap := nil.		].	destMap := nil.! !!CoolingStrategyMap methodsFor: 'as yet unclassified' stamp: 'jmi 3/23/2021 20:17'!smoothCoolingMap: sourceMap destination: destMap	| iFinal iOriginal iNextRow iPreviousRow p1 p10 p11 p12 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9 |	" Top Row"	2 to: width - 1 do: [:x|		iOriginal := x + (0 * width).		iNextRow := iOriginal + width.		iPreviousRow := (height * width) + iOriginal - width.		iFinal := ((sourceMap at: iOriginal - 1) 			+ (sourceMap at: iOriginal)			+ (sourceMap at: iOriginal + 1)			+ (sourceMap at: iPreviousRow)			+ (sourceMap at: iNextRow)) // 5.		destMap at: iOriginal put: iFinal.		].	"All the Middle Rows"	1 to: height - 2 do: [:y|		2 to: width - 1 do: [:x|			"Get the surrounding colors, subtract some amount, average them, then write the result"			iOriginal := x + (y * width).			iNextRow := iOriginal + width.			iPreviousRow := iOriginal - width.			iFinal := ((sourceMap at: iOriginal - 1) 				+ (sourceMap at: iOriginal)				+ (sourceMap at: iOriginal + 1)				+ (sourceMap at: iPreviousRow)				+ (sourceMap at: iNextRow)) // 5.			destMap at: iOriginal put: iFinal.			].		].	"Bottom Row"	2 to: width -1 do: [:x|		iOriginal := x + (height * width) - width.		iNextRow := iOriginal \\ width.		iPreviousRow := iOriginal - width.		iFinal := ((sourceMap at: iOriginal - 1) 			+ (sourceMap at: iOriginal)			+ (sourceMap at: iOriginal + 1)			+ (sourceMap at: iPreviousRow)			+ (sourceMap at: iNextRow)) // 5.		destMap at: iOriginal put: iFinal.		]."I CHANGED THE HEIGHT END CONDITION FROM height-1 TO heiight-2 BUT I'M NOT SURE THAT'S CORRECT"	"The left side"	1 to: height - 2 do: [:y|		"Get the surrounding colors, subtract some amount, average them, then write the result"		iOriginal := 1 + (y *